Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; OPTIONAL managed configuration for Soft Phone (read by the app's PolicyProvider).
;
; The app never ships with a domain — by default every user enters and validates their own
; tenant domain on first run. This template is only for a SINGLE-ORG fleet where an admin
; wants to set THEIR organization's own domain for all their users, so those users skip the
; prompt. Omit it and the app simply asks each user for the domain (the normal behavior).
;
; >>> Set "Domain" to YOUR organization's tenant domain before deploying. <<<
; Deploy via Intune (Devices > Configuration > registry / OMA-URI) or Group Policy.
; AllowUserOverrideDomain=1 makes the domain an editable default instead of a locked value.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\CrestApps\SoftPhone]
"Domain"="your-tenant-domain.example.com"
"AllowUserOverrideDomain"=dword:00000000
"StartWithWindows"=dword:00000001
"RingtoneEnabled"=dword:00000001
